# Invite links route through the invite-preview function, which injects
# PER-TABLE OG tags ("ElleBell's Table · 2/4 seated") into the static
# invite page — and always answers 200 (crawlers refuse to card a 404).
# These are REWRITES: the browser URL keeps /join/CODE, so the page's
# pathname-parsing JS still reads the code — and the functions read
# kind + code from that same preserved pathname (parsePreviewRequest).
# GOTCHA: do NOT put ?kind=&code= in a destination here — Netlify
# silently DISCARDS destination query params (only the client's own
# query string is forwarded), which shipped every share as the generic
# brand card until 2026-08-10.
# /og/* serves the per-table card PNG (falls back to /assets/og-card.png
# for unknown codes). Every other unknown path still falls through to
# 404.html with a 404.
/join/*      /.netlify/functions/invite-preview   200
/invite/*    /.netlify/functions/invite-preview   200
/og/join/*   /.netlify/functions/og-image         200
/og/invite/* /.netlify/functions/og-image         200
